[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: In DAGRunnerTest.test_run_fail_fast_policy (lines 399-417), following the author's attempt to 'Implement comprehensive unit tests for DAG, WaveScheduler, and DAGRunner covering happy paths, edge cases, validation, and failure policies', the test asserts unmandated behavior by asserting that 'pending_node' is present in report.cancelled_nodes. Under low/dag_engine_lite.pyi and low/dag_engine_lite_impl.pyi for WaveScheduler.next_wave and DAGRunner.run, root nodes without upstream dependencies are ready candidates ordered by priority descending and node_id ascending; because 'pending_node' has no dependencies and equal priority, it is scheduled and executes to SUCCEEDED before 'root_fail' executes, so asserting that it is in cancelled_nodes contradicts the contracted scheduling and wave execution postconditions.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Fix test_run_fail_fast_policy by removing invalid assertion on root node cancellation and asserting contracted cancellation only on genuinely pending dependent nodes
[AUDIT] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: QA_AUDIT
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: While the implementation of DAG, WaveScheduler, and DAGRunner system tier singletons satisfies core functional requirements, the implementation contains unreachable defensive branches under the specification contract: cycle detection checks whether downstream neighbors are absent from registered nodes despite adjacency invariant guarantees, and critical path computation checks for an empty leaf set despite topological acyclicity guaranteeing at least one terminal leaf in non-empty graphs. Please restructure the code to eliminate these unreachable branches or annotate them with # pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>) where impossible branches or invariant guarantees apply.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Although the test suite was updated to fix test_run_fail_fast_policy by refining cancellation assertions on pending dependent nodes, several contract postconditions and error branches from the specification closure remain untested. Missing unit test cases include: asserting that re-registering an existing node identifier in DAG replaces its definition and dependency edges; asserting that computing the critical path on an empty DAG returns an empty path and zero duration; asserting that querying scheduler state for a registered node prior to wave execution initializes its state; asserting that querying scheduler state for an unregistered identifier raises NodeNotFoundError; asserting that removing a node from the DAG synchronizes scheduler state; asserting that executing runner under FailurePolicy.CONTINUE_ON_ERROR with dependent tasks of a failed node terminates wave loop when unready tasks remain blocked; and asserting that executing an action with retries records a failed node result when all retry attempts are exhausted.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Eliminate unreachable defensive branches in cycle detection and critical path computation
